# Challenge Center — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Redesign the existing **Progress** tab into a **Challenge Center** screen, faithfully translating the `myada_challenge_center_wireframe.html` into Flutter widgets. This plan covers all six objectives: screen refactor, pixel-perfect translation, theme integration, componentization, mock data layer, and navigation update.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The wireframe's bottom nav shows **4 tabs**: Home, Modules, Challenges, Profile. The current `MainNavShell` has **5 slots**: Home, Ranks (index 1), Learn (FAB at index 2), Progress (index 3), Profile (index 4). We cannot remove the Ranks or Learn screens without breaking navigation.
>
> **Recommended approach:** Keep the existing 5-slot layout. Only update slot #3 (currently "Progress") to "Challenges" with a trophy/star icon. The Ranks tab remains as "Ranks", which is not in the wireframe's 4-tab nav. Confirm this is acceptable, or specify if Ranks should be renamed/removed.

> [!WARNING]
> The wireframe uses several colors not in the current `AppColors` palette — amber `#854f0b`, coral `#993c1d`, purple `#3c3489`, and light variants for icon/pill backgrounds. Per the task rules, strictly new colors will be **added to `app_colors.dart`** under a new `// Challenge Center` section rather than hardcoded in the UI.

